🏎️ Racing Telemetry Analytics Platform

A cloud-based motorsport telemetry analytics system built with Python and AWS.
It processes racing data stored in S3 and provides an interactive dashboard for lap analysis, driver behaviour insights, and performance comparison.

⸻

🚀 Project Overview

This project ingests and analyses telemetry data from an AMG GT3 at Brands Hatch, focusing on:

* Lap-by-lap performance comparison
* Driver input analysis (throttle, brake, RPM)
* Performance scoring system
* Best vs worst lap detection
* Interactive visualisation dashboard

The goal is to simulate a simplified race engineering telemetry system.

⸻

☁️ Cloud Architecture

Data is stored in:

* Amazon Web Services S3

Pipeline flow:

1. Load telemetry CSV from S3
2. Clean and validate dataset
3. Aggregate by lap
4. Compute performance metrics
5. Visualise results in Streamlit dashboard

⸻

🧠 Key Features

* AWS S3 data ingestion
* Multi-lap telemetry analysis
* Driver performance scoring model
* Best vs worst lap comparison
* Race engineering insights engine
* Interactive Streamlit dashboard

⸻

🏁 Motorsport Context

The analytics approach is inspired by real-world race engineering workflows used in professional motorsport, including systems similar in concept to those used by Mercedes-AMG Petronas Formula One Team.

⸻

🧰 Tech Stack

* Python
* Pandas
* Streamlit
* Boto3 (AWS SDK)
* Matplotlib

⸻

📁 Project Structure

racing-telemetry-project/
│
├── app.py                  # Streamlit dashboard
├── cloud_test.py          # AWS / data debugging script
├── requirements.txt       # Dependencies
├── README.md              # Documentation
│
├── src/
│   ├── data_loader.py     # AWS S3 data ingestion
│   ├── analysis.py        # Lap analysis & scoring
│   └── insights.py        # Engineering insights
│
└── data/                  # Optional local dataset

▶️ How to Run

Install dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

Run Dashboard

streamlit run app.py

⸻

☁️ AWS Setup

This project uses Amazon Web Services S3 for storing and loading telemetry data.

To run this project locally, you will need to set up your own S3 bucket and upload the dataset.

⸻

📦 1. Create an S3 Bucket

Create a bucket in AWS S3:

* Name: any name you choose (e.g. your-telemetry-bucket)
* Region: your preferred region

Upload your telemetry CSV file into the bucket.

⸻

📄 2. Upload Dataset

Upload a file with the same structure as the project expects, for example:
AMGGT3-BRANDSHATCH.csv

Make sure it contains telemetry columns such as:

* rpm
* throttle
* brake
* lapNum

⸻

🔐 3. Configure AWS Credentials

Before running the project, configure your AWS credentials locally:

aws configure

You will be prompted for:

* AWS Access Key ID
* AWS Secret Access Key
* Default region name
* Output format

These credentials must belong to an IAM user with permission to access S3.

⸻

🛡️ 4. Required IAM Permissions

Ensure your IAM user has at least:

* s3:GetObject
* s3:ListBucket

⸻

⚙️ 5. Update Project Configuration

In app.py and cloud_test.py, set:

BUCKET_NAME = "your-bucket-name"
FILE_NAME = "your-file-name.csv" example: (AMGGT3-BRANDSHATCH.csv)

